            {
              "id": "c2fef91c-dd5a-4d45-9f8e-0f4b456c515d",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Anthropolgy of Performance</strong></em> is a collection of essays written by Victor Turner, published posthumously by PAJ Publications, June 1, 1988."
            },
            {
              "id": "2bca76b7-a972-4297-b7e8-87952cc7581c",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "e56af173-27a1-4f08-b509-94048fa3fc45",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Turner is all over the globe as he addresses issues of cultural performance, </em><a href=\"#/in-tune-with-the-world\"><em>carnival</em></a><em>, film, theatre, and &quot;performing ethnography&quot; to break new ground in anthropological thinking about event, spectacle, and audience. One of his last writings, &quot;Body, Brain, and Culture&quot; links cerebral neurology and anthropology studies in a fascinating interface.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
